171	/**
172	 * Assigns the owner's deterministic {@code householdId}: the first 12 hex characters of SHA-256 over
173	 * {@code normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode}. The household is therefore keyed on
174	 * (last name, postcode) alone, so any two owners with the same last name and postcode share the same
175	 * id automatically — nothing has to opt in and no existing owner is mutated. {@code sharesHousehold}
176	 * no longer creates the link; it only lets {@link CheckOwnerIdentityUnique} wave through the
177	 * otherwise-blocked household duplicate. Runs on the create pipeline before the duplicate check and
178	 * before {@link SaveOwner}, so the stored id, the duplicate detection and the household-size count
179	 * all read the same computed value.
